@startuml buffer-page-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' Buffer-pool PAGE (frame) lifecycle, PART 1 of 2 — the TOP-LEVEL cycle: how one
' 256 KB block-storage page moves between disk and a buffer-pool frame and back
' out again (fault-in · write-back · CLOCK victim eviction). The Resident state's
' internal Clean/Dirty × Pinned/Unpinned substates are the companion figure
' buffer-page-lifecycle-2.puml (PART 2).
'
' Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/core/buffer_manager.rs
'   A `Frame` carries  block_id · lease_state (read-pin count | WRITE_LEASE) ·
'   dirty flag · reference_bit (CLOCK second-chance).  There is no literal
'   `enum PageState`; the lifecycle is the product of
'     {resident, on-disk} × {clean, dirty} × {pinned, unpinned}.
'   Operations:  load_page / pin_page_data (fault-in) · pin_read / pin_write ·
'   unpin_read / unpin_write · mark_dirty (on write) · flush_page / flush_all
'   (write-back → clear_dirty) · get_free_frame (CLOCK victim eviction).
'   Invariants enforced by the code:
'     · a frame is NOT evictable while pinned (any read lease or the write lease);
'     · a dirty frame may NOT be flushed while a WRITE_LEASE is held;
'     · the CLOCK victim must be unpinned AND have reference_bit == 0;
'     · a dirty victim is written back (clear_dirty) before its frame is reused.
'
' Color key:
'   green (#C8E6C9) = page is RESIDENT in a buffer-pool frame (in memory)
'   amber (#FFE0B2) = transient control action (fault-in / write-back I/O)
'   blue  (#BBDEFB) = page lives only ON DISK (no resident frame)
'   grey  (#ECEFF1) = empty / free frame slot (infrastructure)
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 210
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title Buffer-pool page (frame) lifecycle (1 of 2)\ntop-level cycle: Disk ⇄ Resident ⇄ eviction

state "On disk\n(no resident frame)" as Disk #BBDEFB : durable block;\nblock_id + location

state "Fault-in\nload_page / pin_page_data" as FaultIn #FFE0B2 : read_block_fixed →\nfree CLOCK frame

state "Resident\n(buffer-pool frame)" as Resident #C8E6C9 : Clean/Dirty × Pinned/Unpinned;\ninternal substates in PART 2\n(buffer-page-lifecycle-2)

state "Write-back\n(victim was dirty)" as WriteBack #FFE0B2 : write_block_fixed\n→ clear_dirty

Disk -[#1565C0]-> FaultIn : miss\n(not in page_table)
FaultIn --> Resident : populated
Resident -[#1565C0]-> WriteBack : victim DIRTY\n(get_free_frame)
WriteBack -[#1565C0]-> Disk : frame detached
Resident -[#1565C0]-> Disk : victim CLEAN\n→ reuse as-is

note bottom of Resident #ECEFF1
  CLOCK (second-chance) reuse in get_free_frame:
  a frame is a candidate only when **unpinned**;
  a set reference_bit grants one reprieve (cleared,
  hand advances); a dirty victim is written back
  first so no acknowledged bytes are lost.
end note

legend right
| Color | Page condition |
|<#C8E6C9>| resident in a buffer-pool frame |
|<#FFE0B2>| fault-in / write-back I/O (transient) |
|<#BBDEFB>| on disk only (no resident frame) |
endlegend
@enduml
